<span>Purpose: Prove that centralization is real BEFORE building the Hat model on it.</span>
<span>Status: Spec complete. Executor generates code from this.</span>
<span></span>
<span><span class="token title important"><span class="token punctuation">##</span> Why denial tests, not happy-path tests</span></span>
<span>A happy-path test passes when authorization is broken but permissive.</span>
<span>A denial test fails loudly when authorization is broken. Since you have zero</span>
<span>integration tests, denial tests are the highest-value first investment: they</span>
<span>are parameterized (cheap per endpoint) and they produce a regression net that</span>
<span>protects every subsequent refactor.</span>
<span></span>
<span><span class="token title important"><span class="token punctuation">##</span> Test taxonomy (7 classes — every endpoint gets at least classes 1, 2, 6)</span></span>
<span></span>
<span><span class="token table"><span class="token table-header-row"><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-header important"> Class </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-header important"> Name </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-header important"> Asserts </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-header important"> Applies to </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span></span></span></span>
<span><span class="token table-line"><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token punctuation">---</span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token punctuation">---</span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token punctuation">---</span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token punctuation">---</span><span class="token punctuation">|</span></span></span>
<span><span class="token table-data-rows"><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> D1 </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Unauthenticated denial </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> No identity → 401 </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Every endpoint </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span></span></span>
<span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> D2 </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Wrong-tenant denial </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Valid identity, other tenant's resource ID → 403/404 </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Every tenant-scoped endpoint </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span></span>
<span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> D3 </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Wrong-hat denial </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Valid identity, valid tenant, insufficient capacity → 403 </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Every capability-gated endpoint </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span></span>
<span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> D4 </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Expired-hat denial </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Hat.valid_until in past → 403 </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Every capability-gated endpoint </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span></span>
<span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> D5 </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Consent-revoked denial </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Valid hat, revoked ConsentGrant → 403 </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Every consent-scoped read/write </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span></span>
<span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> D6 </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Public-projection denial </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Authenticated user requests private field via public route → field absent </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Every public route </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span></span>
<span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> D7 </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Worker-scope denial </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Worker processes message outside its tenant scope → rejected + dead-lettered </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span><span class="token table-data"> Every worker </span><span class="token punctuation">|</span></span>
<span></span>
<span><span class="token title important"><span class="token punctuation">##</span> Test case generation rules</span></span>
<span></span>
<span><span class="token title important"><span class="token punctuation">###</span> Rule G1 — Endpoint table is the source</span></span>
<span>Generate one test per (endpoint × applicable class). Do not hand-write.</span>
<span>The parameterization source is <span class="token code-snippet code keyword">`01-code-reality-map.md`</span> §E3.</span>
<span></span>
<span><span class="token title important"><span class="token punctuation">###</span> Rule G2 — Fixtures are deterministic</span></span>
<span>Three tenants (T1, T2, T3), three persons, three hats per person, fixed GUIDs.</span>
<span>No random data. Every test uses the same seed so failures are reproducible.</span>
<span></span>
<span><span class="token title important"><span class="token punctuation">###</span> Rule G3 — Assert on status AND side-effect</span></span>
<span>For every denial, assert (a) the HTTP status, and (b) that no row was written</span>
<span>to the target table. A test that only checks status will miss write-then-forbid bugs.</span>
<span></span>
<span><span class="token title important"><span class="token punctuation">###</span> Rule G4 — Denial must not leak existence</span></span>
<span>For cross-tenant access, the response must be identical whether the resource</span>
<span>exists in another tenant or does not exist at all. Assert byte-equality of</span>
<span>the response body. This is the IDOR-leak test.</span>
<span></span>
<span><span class="token title important"><span class="token punctuation">##</span> C# skeleton (Executor expands this)</span></span>
<span></span>
<span>```csharp</span>
<span>[Collection("authorization")]</span>
<span>public class AuthorizationDenialTests(TestHost host, Fixtures fx) : IClassFixture<span class="token tag"><span class="token tag"><span class="token punctuation">&lt;</span>TestHost</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></span></span>
<span>{</span>
<span>    public static IEnumerable<span class="token tag"><span class="token tag"><span class="token punctuation">&lt;</span>object[]</span><span class="token punctuation">&gt;</span></span> TenantScopedEndpoints =&gt; EndpointCatalog.TenantScoped();</span>
<span></span>
<span><span class="token code keyword">    [Theory, MemberData(nameof(TenantScopedEndpoints))]</span></span>
<span>    public async Task D1_Unauthenticated_IsDenied(EndpointCase c)</span>
<span>    {</span>
<span>        var res = await host.Anonymous().SendAsync(c.Request(fx.TenantA));</span>
<span>        Assert.Equal(HttpStatusCode.Unauthorized, res.StatusCode);</span>
<span>    }</span>
<span></span>
<span><span class="token code keyword">    [Theory, MemberData(nameof(TenantScopedEndpoints))]</span></span>
<span>    public async Task D2_CrossTenant_IsDenied_AndDoesNotLeakExistence(EndpointCase c)</span>
<span>    {</span>
<span>        var asA = host.As(fx.PersonA);</span>
<span>        var real = await asA.SendAsync(c.Request(fx.ResourceInTenantB));</span>
<span>        var fake = await asA.SendAsync(c.Request(fx.NonExistentResource));</span>
