<span># ARTIFACT 03 — `03-entity-ledger.md`</span>
<span></span>
<span>```markdown</span>
<span># Entity Ledger v2.0</span>
<span>Purpose: Single source of truth for every entity, its owner, its lifecycle,</span>
<span>and its disposition from v1.1. Target: 25 aggregates, ~70 total entities.</span>
<span></span>
<span>## 1. Aggregate Roots (25)</span>
<span></span>
<span>An aggregate root is the only entry point for transactional writes to its</span>
<span>cluster. No module reads another module's tables.</span>
<span></span>
<span>| New ID | Aggregate | Module | Owns | Concurrency | Key invariant |</span>
<span>|---|---|---|---|---|---|</span>
<span>| A-01 | Person | Identity | Login, passkeys, MFA, locale | Optimistic (rowversion) | — |</span>
<span>| A-02 | Organization | Org Graph | Legal identity, domains, registry IDs, status, parent/child via A-09 | Optimistic | One canonical record across both sites |</span>
<span>| A-03 | Workspace | Org Graph | Tenant boundary, region, billing owner, policy | Optimistic | Every private record has exactly one owning workspace (I-06) |</span>
<span>| A-04 | Membership | Identity | Person×Org standing, baseline rights | Optimistic | Baseline only; never grants scoped authority |</span>
<span>| A-05 | Hat | Identity | Person×Org×ChannelRecipeInstance×Capacity×Scope×Validity | Optimistic | Hat ≤ Agreement policy (I-04); Persona never grants |</span>
<span>| A-06 | ChannelRecipeInstance | Programs | Recipe version binding + org overrides + EffectiveConfig | Optimistic | Recipe version immutable once bound |</span>
<span>| A-07 | DirectoryListing | Directory | Public face, field provenance, freshness | Optimistic | Public listing ≠ permission to publish relationship (I-01) |</span>
<span>| A-08 | Program | Programs | Pinned BlueprintVersion, effective config, revision | Optimistic + revision | Blueprint immutable (I-02); change never silent (I-03) |</span>
<span>| A-09 | Relationship | Org Graph | Typed, directed, time-bound org link, disclosure setting | Optimistic | Typed: parent/division/franchise/partner/competitor |</span>
<span>| A-10 | CollaborationAgreement | Agreements | Parties, sharing policy, terms, retention | Optimistic | Sharing only through active Agreement (SR-03) |</span>
<span>| A-11 | EvidenceRecord | Evidence | Sourced claim + provenance + expiry + audience | Optimistic | Provenance and expiry mandatory |</span>
<span>| A-12 | PassportShare | Evidence | Evidence×Recipient×Purpose×Expiry | Optimistic | Revocation blocks new use immediately (I-05) |</span>
<span>| A-13 | ConsentGrant | Agreements | Subject×Scope×Audience×Purpose×Expiry×Revocation | Optimistic | Purpose-scoped, revocable (SR-04) |</span>
<span>| A-14 | Introduction | Journeys | Brief, status, SLA, participants | Optimistic | Double opt-in required (J-02) |</span>
<span>| A-15 | JourneyInstance | Journeys | Journey ref, version, state, participants, milestones | Optimistic + state machine | Engine-agnostic; every transition audited |</span>
<span>| A-16 | Opportunity | Revenue | Pursuit, participants, contributions | Optimistic | — |</span>
<span>| A-17 | DealRegistration | Revenue | Claim, policy version, decision, appeal | Optimistic | Precedence by policy, never hard-coded timestamp (I-07) |</span>
<span>| A-18 | AttributionDecision | Revenue | Versioned credit allocation + evidence | Optimistic | Separate from entitlement (I-09) |</span>
<span>| A-19 | FinancialJournal | Revenue | Balanced entries, reversals, reconciliation | Append-only + reversal | Decimal+currency, never float (I-10) |</span>
<span>| A-20 | ContentCard | Content | Type, schema version, data, locale, status, provenance | Optimistic | Card never owns placement |</span>
<span>| A-21 | ContentPage | Content | Layout, card refs, SEO metadata, locale | Optimistic | Page never owns card content |</span>
<span>| A-22 | Publication | Content | Target, state, schedule, version | Optimistic | SEO gates apply here only |</span>
<span>| A-23 | IntegrationConnection | Integrations | Credential ref, mappings, sync state | Optimistic | Credentials are refs, never rows (SR-08) |</span>
<span>| A-24 | Subscription | Billing | Plan, entitlement keys, usage | Optimistic | Entitlements checked in domain layer, not UI |</span>
<span>| A-25 | AgentPrincipal | Identity | Issuer, scopes, expiry, bound Hat, max scope | Optimistic | Delegated scopes only, never full session (SR-10) |</span>
<span></span>
<span>## 2. Associative Objects (first-class, own lifecycle, not aggregates)</span>
<span></span>
<span>| ID | Object | Links | Why first-class | Owner module |</span>
<span>|---|---|---|---|---|</span>
<span>| H-02 | Membership (=A-04) | Person × Org × Workspace | Multi-org membership is normal | Identity |</span>
<span>| H-01 | Hat (=A-05) | Person × Org × RecipeInstance × Capacity × Scope | Authorization subject; multi-hat = multiple rows | Identity |</span>
<span>| H-03 | Relationship (=A-09) | Org × Org (typed) | Org hierarchies without special-casing | Org Graph |</span>
<span>| H-04 | AgreementParty | Agreement × Org × sharing scope | Agreements may have &gt;2 parties | Agreements |</span>
<span>| H-05 | ProgramEnrollment | Org × Program × RecipeInstance × tier × terms | One org, many programs | Programs |</span>
<span>| H-06 | HatDelegation | Hat × Hat (delegate) × expiry | Delegate-of-delegate needs a ceiling (see G-A4) | Identity |</span>
<span>| H-07 | CardPlacement | Card × Page × position | Cards are reused across pages | Content |</span>
<span></span>
<span>## 3. Immutable Entities (identified, never mutated; new version = new row)</span>
<span></span>
<span>| ID | Entity | Module | Why immutable |</span>
<span>|---|---|---|---|</span>
<span>| I-01 | BlueprintVersion | Programs | Programs pin a version (I-02) |</span>
<span>| I-02 | ChannelRecipe | Programs | Versioned composition (Artifact 08) |</span>
<span>| I-03 | JourneyDefinition | Journeys | YAML compiled; versioned by content hash |</span>
<span>| I-04 | PolicyVersion | Authorization | Every decision cites a policy version |</span>
<span>| I-05 | VerticalPack | Programs | Configuration bundle |</span>
<span>| I-06 | Explorer | Content | Query definition + presentation config |</span>
<span>| I-07 | ToolDefinition | Integrations | Named Tool + JSON schema + version (see G-A20) |</span>
<span></span>
<span>## 4. Derived / Projections (rebuildable, never authoritative)</span>
<span></span>
<span>| ID | Projection | Source of truth | Rebuild trigger |</span>
<span>|---|---|---|---|</span>
<span>| P-01 | InboxItem | JourneyInstance + WorkItem | Journey transition |</span>
<span>| P-02 | MatchRecommendation | Listing facts + scoring config | Fact change or config change |</span>
<span>| P-03 | EffectiveConfigView | ChannelRecipeInstance | Reconfiguration |</span>
<span>| P-04 | PublicProjection (per entity type) | Approved fields only | Publication event |</span>
<span>| P-05 | PartnerHealthSignal | Journey milestones | Milestone event |</span>
<span>| P-06 | SearchIndex | PublicProjection | Publication event |</span>
<span></span>
<span>Rule: a projection may be deleted and rebuilt at any time. If deleting it loses</span>
<span>information, it was not a projection.</span>
<span></span>
<span>## 5. Value Objects (no identity, immutable)</span>
<span></span>
<span>| VO | Used by | Definition |</span>
<span>|---|---|---|</span>
<span>| Money | A-19, A-24 | decimal(19,4) + ISO 4217 currency |</span>
<span>| Provenance | A-07, A-11, A-20 | {source, sourceDate, reviewer, trustLabel, verifiedAt} |</span>
<span>| TrustLabel | Provenance | Enum: CompanyAsserted, DocumentReviewed, RegistryChecked, CounterpartyConfirmed, Expired, Disputed |</span>
<span>| EffectiveConfig | A-06, A-08 | {resolvedJson, hash, layers[], lockedFields[]} |</span>
<span>| SlaTimer | A-14, A-15 | {duration, startedAt, pausedAt?, breachedAt?} |</span>
<span>| Scope | A-05, A-12, A-13, A-25 | Enum: WholeOrg, OneProgram, OneRelationship, OneJourney |</span>
<span>| Capacity | A-05 | Enum: OrgAdmin, ProgramSponsor, ProgramPartner, RelationshipParticipant, Buyer, Reviewer, Delegate |</span>
<span>| PurposeCode | A-12, A-13 | Controlled taxonomy — see G-A11 |</span>
<span>| Hash | A-15, A-22, I-03, I-04 | SHA-256 over canonical JSON |</span>
<span></span>
<span>## 6. Reconciliation Table — v1.1 IDs → v2.0 disposition</span>
<span></span>
<span>Every v1.1 entity is accounted for. Nothing silently dropped.</span>
<span></span>
<span>| v1.1 ID | v1.1 Name | v2.0 Disposition | Rationale |</span>
<span>|---|---|---|---|</span>
<span>| A-01 | Person | → A-01 Person | Unchanged |</span>
<span>| A-02 | Organization | → A-02 Organization | Unchanged |</span>
<span>| A-03 | Membership | → A-04 + H-02 | Reclassified as associative |</span>
<span>| A-04 | Workspace | → A-03 Workspace | Renumbered |</span>
<span>| A-05 | Hat | → A-05 + H-01 | Reclassified as associative; added ChannelRecipeInstanceId + Validity |</span>
<span>| A-06 | Persona | → **Reference data, not an entity** | Persona is a UX profile resolved from Hat; it has no lifecycle, no identity, no writes. Store as a static config table. |</span>
<span>| A-07 | DirectoryListing | → A-07 | Unchanged; provenance made mandatory |</span>
<span>| A-08 | Program | → A-08 | Unchanged |</span>
<span>| A-09 | BlueprintVersion | → I-01 (immutable entity) | Immutable by invariant I-02; no transactional conflicts |</span>
<span>| A-10 | Inbox | → P-01 (projection) | Rebuildable from JourneyInstance; holding it as an aggregate caused the "inbox owns tasks" confusion |</span>
<span>| A-11 | Relationship | → A-09 + H-03 | Reclassified as associative; typed |</span>
<span>| A-12 | CollaborationAgreement | → A-10 + H-04 | Split: agreement vs party |</span>
<span>| A-13 | EvidenceRecord | → A-11 | Unchanged; added audience field |</span>
<span>| A-14 | PassportShare | → A-12 | Unchanged |</span>
<span>| A-15 | ConsentGrant | → A-13 | Unchanged; PurposeCode made controlled |</span>
<span>| A-16 | Introduction | → A-14 | Unchanged; SLA moved to shared SlaTimer VO |</span>
<span>| A-17 | Journey | → A-15 JourneyInstance | Split from JourneyDefinition (I-03) |</span>
<span>| A-18 | Opportunity | → A-16 | Unchanged |</span>
<span>| A-19 | DealRegistration | → A-17 | Unchanged; policyVersion made mandatory |</span>
<span>| A-20 | AttributionDecision | → A-18 | Unchanged |</span>
<span>| A-21 | FinancialJournal | → A-19 | Unchanged; append-only enforced |</span>
<span>| A-22 | ContentCard | → A-20 | Unchanged |</span>
<span>| A-23 | ContentPage | → A-21 + H-07 CardPlacement | Split: page vs placement |</span>
<span>| A-24 | Publication | → A-22 | Unchanged; became the ONLY SEO gate point |</span>
<span>| A-25 | IntegrationConnection | → A-23 + I-07 ToolDefinition | Split: connection vs exposed tool |</span>
<span>| A-26 | Subscription/Entitlement | → A-24 | Merged (entitlement had no independent lifecycle) |</span>
<span>| A-27 | AgentPrincipal | → A-25 | Added maxScope ceiling (G-A10) |</span>
<span>| A-28 | MatchRecommendation | → P-02 (projection) | Derived; caching it as an aggregate caused staleness bugs |</span>
<span>| A-29 | ProgramEnrollment | → H-05 | Reclassified as associative |</span>
<span></span>
<span>**Net effect:** 29 v1.1 entities → 25 aggregates + 7 associative + 7 immutable</span>
<span>+ 6 projections + 10 value objects. The 265 "tables" in the original inventory</span>
<span>collapse because most were either projections, join tables, or denormalized</span>
<span>copies. No capability is lost.</span>
<span></span>
<span>## 7. Entity count justification</span>
<span>If someone asks "why 25 and not 60?" the answer is: an aggregate root must have</span>
<span>an independent transactional lifecycle AND an invariant that requires</span>
<span>atomicity. Everything else is either a child entity, a projection, or a value.</span>
<span>The 25 above are the only things with their own concurrency boundary.</span>
