<span>- AP-1: `maxScope ≤ boundHat.scope`. Always.</span>
<span>- AP-2: `capabilities ⊆ capabilities(boundHat)`.</span>
<span>- AP-3: `expiresAt ≤ boundHat.validUntil` and `≤ now + 24h`.</span>
<span>- AP-4: `canDelegate` is always false. Agents never mint agents.</span>
<span>- AP-5: Every agent action is logged with `agentPrincipalId` + `boundHatId`.</span>
<span></span>
<span>## 7. Hat expiry mid-journey (closing G-A19)</span>
<span></span>
<span>If a Hat expires while a JourneyInstance is active:</span>
<span>1. The PDP immediately denies new actions for that Hat.</span>
<span>2. The JourneyInstance is **not** cancelled. It transitions to a `blocked`</span>
<span>   audit state.</span>
<span>3. A notification goes to the Organization's OrgAdmin Hats to reassign.</span>
<span>4. On reassignment, the journey resumes with a new Hat ID; the audit record</span>
<span>   shows the substitution.</span>
<span>5. If no reassignment within the gate timeout, the journey's `on_expire`</span>
<span>   fires normally.</span>
<span></span>
<span>**Never** auto-extend a Hat. Extension is an explicit OrgAdmin action.</span>
<span></span>
