<span>**Hard rule:** no vendor type ever leaves the Infrastructure folder. The domain</span>
<span>layer sees only internal contracts (anti-corruption layer).</span>
<span></span>
<span>## 2. The 10 mandatory contract fields (from v1.1 §12) — expanded</span>
<span></span>
<span>| # | Field | Where declared | Example |</span>
<span>|---|---|---|---|</span>
<span>| 1 | System of record per object/field | `mapping.yaml` | `Opportunity.amount` owned by CRM; `JourneyInstance` owned by us |</span>
<span>| 2 | Stable external identity mapping | `identity-map.yaml` | `CRM.AccountId ↔ Organization.Id` (immutable) |</span>
<span>| 3 | Deduplication policy | `mapping.yaml` | Match on domain + registry ID; never on name |</span>
<span>| 4 | Update precedence | `mapping.yaml` | CRM wins on amount; we win on relationship type |</span>
<span>| 5 | Loop prevention + correlation IDs | `sync-policy.yaml` | Every outbound carries `correlationId`; inbound with known correlation is ignored |</span>
<span>| 6 | Delete / tombstone handling | `sync-policy.yaml` | CRM delete → we soft-delete and record provenance; never hard-delete |</span>
<span>| 7 | Retry + dead-letter behavior | `sync-policy.yaml` | 5 retries exponential 1s→16s; then DLQ + alert |</span>
<span>| 8 | Reconciliation report | `recon.yaml` | Daily: count by object, drift list, unmatched |</span>
<span>| 9 | Credential expiry + disconnect behavior | `auth.yaml` | Expiry → notify OrgAdmin 7d prior; on expiry, queue writes, don't drop |</span>
<span>| 10 | Customer-visible error ownership | `errors.yaml` | Which errors are ours to fix vs theirs to fix vs vendor outage |</span>
<span></span>
<span>## 3. Tool exposure (closing G-A20)</span>
<span></span>
<span>Journeys never call HTTP. They call **Tools**.</span>
