<span># ARTIFACT 11 — `11-gap-register.md`</span>
<span></span>
<span>```markdown</span>
<span># Gap Register v2.0</span>
<span>Purpose: Every gap found during the upgrade, with resolution and owner.</span>
<span>20 gaps. Gaps marked [OPEN] require a decision from the founder.</span>
<span></span>
<span>| ID | Gap | Severity | Resolution | Artifact | Status |</span>
<span>|---|---|---|---|---|---|</span>
<span>| G-A1 | No authorization/integration tests exist | **Critical** | D1–D8 denial suite, parameterized over endpoint inventory | 02 | Resolved by 02 |</span>
<span>| G-A2 | Journeys had no engine binding | High | `execution_hints` block required in every YAML | 04 §0 | Resolved |</span>
<span>| G-A3 | No correlation key between JourneyInstance and audit | High | `workflow_instance_id` = `JourneyInstance.Id` | 10 §7 | Resolved |</span>
<span>| G-A4 | Delegation had no depth ceiling (infinite chain risk) | High | `depth ≤ 2`; HD-1..HD-5 invariants | 07 §8 | Resolved |</span>
<span>| G-A5 | Consent revocation vs candidate generation untested | High | D5 tests + consent check at candidate generation (not just at read) | 02, 07 | Resolved |</span>
<span>| G-A6 | ChannelRecipe migration had no rollback | High | `migrationHistory` snapshot; 30-day rollback window | 08 §3 | Resolved |</span>
<span>| G-A7 | Unpublish had no named owner | Medium | Publication.Archived requires Editor role | 06 §4 | Resolved |</span>
<span>| G-A8 | Cross-org journey: which workspace owns the instance? | **High** | **Owner = the workspace of the triggering Hat.** Participants access via Agreement. | 03 A-15, 04 | Resolved |</span>
<span>| G-A9 | Two SLA timers for the same introduction | Medium | Single `SlaTimer` VO on A-14; journey reads, never creates | 04 J-02 note | Resolved |</span>
<span>| G-A10 | AgentPrincipal had no scope ceiling | **High** | `maxScope`, AP-1..AP-5 invariants | 07 §6 | Resolved |</span>
<span>| G-A11 | Evidence "purpose" was free text (breaks matching) | High | `PurposeCode` controlled taxonomy | 03 VO, 07 | **Resolved — taxonomy needs drafting** |</span>
<span>| G-A12 | Conflict policy version changes mid-flight | Medium | `DealRegistration.policyVersion` frozen at submit | 03 A-17, 04 J-05 | Resolved |</span>
<span>| G-A13 | Compensation actions can themselves fail | Medium | `CompensationRegistry` requires idempotency; failures escalate | 04 §4 | Resolved |</span>
<span>| G-A14 | Audit survives tenant deletion but holds tenant-derived hashes | Medium | Hashes only, never payloads; legal hold flag | 10 §8 | Resolved |</span>
<span>| G-A15 | SEO gate threshold unspecified | Low | Initial: ≥10 profiles + ≥150 words; tune at 90d | 06 §7 | **Resolved as [A]** |</span>
<span>| G-A16 | Public projection staleness unbounded | Medium | Publication event → rebuild ≤60s; sitemap hourly | 06 §7 | Resolved |</span>
<span>| G-A17 | No idempotency spec for journey transitions | **High** | Every transition carries an idempotency key; D8 test class | 02, 04 | **Resolved — add D8 to 02** |</span>
<span>| G-A18 | 11 personas, no capability mapping | **High** | Persona→capacity table; PersonaResolver deterministic | 07 §5 | Resolved |</span>
<span>| G-A19 | Hat expiring mid-journey undefined | **High** | Journey blocks (not cancels); OrgAdmin notified; no auto-extend | 07 §7 | Resolved |</span>
<span>| G-A20 | Tool schemas had no versioning | Medium | `ToolDefinition.version`; journeys pin versions | 09 §3 | Resolved |</span>
<span></span>
<span>## Deferred gaps (accepted risk, not resolved)</span>
<span></span>
<span>| ID | Gap | Why deferred | Trigger to revisit |</span>
<span>|---|---|---|---|</span>
<span>| G-D1 | No disaster-recovery test | Cost; do before launch | Before first paying customer |</span>
<span>| G-D2 | No relevance golden set | Need traffic first | At 100 introductions |</span>
<span>| G-D3 | Trademark clearance | Legal cost | Before any marketing spend |</span>
<span>| G-D4 | EU AI Act timeline | Amending; needs counsel | Before EU launch |</span>
<span>| G-D5 | Pricing untested | Need interviews | At 20 interviews |</span>
<span></span>
<span>## Gaps that remain genuinely open — need founder decision</span>
<span></span>
<span>| ID | Question | Options | Impact if unresolved |</span>
<span>|---|---|---|---|</span>
<span>| **G-O1** | Which PurposeCode taxonomy? (G-A11) | (a) Adopt a standard (e.g., DPV) (b) Draft a 12-code custom list (c) Derive from evidence types | Consent matching cannot be implemented |</span>
<span>| **G-O2** | Which workspace owns a JourneyInstance when the trigger is a Buyer Hat but the work happens in a Sponsor workspace? (G-A8) | (a) Triggering Hat's workspace (b) Sponsor's workspace always (c) Explicit `ownerWorkspaceId` at creation | Every cross-org journey needs this |</span>
<span>| **G-O3** | Is J-05 really stateless, or does the 5-day appeal window force it to Layer 1? (G-A9 related) | (a) Stateless with a scheduled sweep closing windows (b) Move to Windmill at launch | Determines whether Windmill ships in month 2 or month 4 |</span>
